<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA ARTROM'S 1996 PROFIT UP SLIGHTLY.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA ARTROM'S 1996 PROFIT UP SLIGHTLY.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (billion of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross profit			     1.58     vs     1.02</p>
<p> Net profit				 1.58     vs     1.02</p>
<p> Turnover				  73.44     vs    40.61</p>
<p> Fixed assets			   176.82     vs   164.73</p>
<p> Current assets			  42.05     vs    32.29</p>
<p> Total assets			   304.57     vs   245.30</p>
<p> Share capital			  141.33     vs   141.33</p>
<p> Total debts			    156.53     vs   101.13</p>
<p> Total dividends			565 million    vs    n.a.</p>
<p> Dividend per share - net	     90 lei   vs    n.a.</p>
<p>NOTE -- Artrom is a state-run engineering company listed on the second tier of the Bucharest stock exchange. Data, reported to the bourse, are in nominal terms and in line with Romanian accounting standards. ($=7,090 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
